english_words.txt.gz: the lowercase entries (no proper nouns) of the "american-english" and "british-english"
word lists from SCOWL (Spell Checker Oriented Word Lists), as shipped by Debian's wamerican and wbritish packages
(British spellings cover Canadian ones such as "cheque", "programme", "neighbourhood"). Used by layer2/normalize.py so that
real English words are never "corrected".

